<Folder><name>Food</name>
<Placemark><name>Ají Limón by Nelly</name><description><![CDATA[Peruvian / Asian fusion · Santander · €€<br>Small neighbourhood restaurant (about four tables) blending Peruvian and Asian flavours. Dishes named by one listing: corvina ceviche, Korean potatoes, chaufa rice, steak tartare and the Peruanito shredded-beef sandwich. About €30 per person before drinks.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/sgpokoteUTUyuAAX8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#aji-limon-by-nelly">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.7984119,43.4691113,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Alterna Sidrería (Calle Rosal)</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Oviedo, Asturias · 984 08 64 35<br>Traditional Asturian cider house opened in Oviedo in 2016 (founders Carlos Pedrouzo and Mònica Gallo), serving traditional Asturian dishes with ciders poured by escanciadores. Member of the Sidrerías de Asturias quality brand; Tripadvisor Travellers' Choice 2023.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3600215,-5.8469674">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#alterna-sidreria-calle-rosal">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.8469674,43.3600215,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Alterna Sidrería (Puerto de Pajares)</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Oviedo, Asturias · 984 28 06 41<br>Second Alterna location (Alterna Teatinos) in Oviedo: traditional Asturian cuisine and cider poured by escanciadores; Sidrerías de Asturias quality brand.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/cDDL3gzK3sn4hCz59">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#alterna-sidreria-puerto-de-pajares">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.8360637,43.3712341,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Asador Llorente</name><description><![CDATA[Asador (grill) · Potes, Liébana · €€ · 942 738 165<br>Traditional Cantabrian grill restaurant in Potes with a rustic wood-paneled dining room and mountain views, known for red meat (chuletón) and its cocido lebaniego, described as the star of the menu. About 100 km from Santander, on the Picos / Liébana side.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.154093,-4.621832">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#asador-llorente">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.621832,43.154093,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Atypique</name><description><![CDATA[Café / breakfast · Santander (centre) · €€ · +34 661 17 92 56<br>Pet-friendly specialty coffee shop in the ground floor of the Siboney building, redesigned by Zooco Estudio; pastries and international breakfast/brunch dishes (avocado toast, acai bowls, chia pudding, vegan banana bread) with a terrace over the marina.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/eUHFZLQccPbFRLaA8?g_st=ic">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#atypique">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.794985,43.463228,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Azabache</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Mompía, Santa Cruz de Bezana<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/VXVyKdEz8nKz3dtx8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#azabache">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.919483,43.4330936,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bodega del Riojano</name><description><![CDATA[Traditional Cantabrian · Santander · €€–€€€ · 942 216 750<br>Historic central Santander restaurant known as 'Museo Redondo' for its dining room of painted wine-barrel ends. Traditional product-led cooking: daily fish, spoon dishes, tripe, snails, cuttlefish in ink, cabracho pie and ensaladilla. Mid-range, historic, and great for Cantabrian food.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.464116,-3.804221">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#bodega-del-riojano">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.804221,43.464116,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bodega Fuente Dé</name><description><![CDATA[Tapas &amp; pintxos · Santander · 942 21 30 58<br>Long-standing Santander bodega serving tapas and cheese plates with wine and beer; known for its cocido montañés, cheese and croquetas. Often packed, with standing room at the bar.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.463455,-3.799276">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#bodega-fuente-de">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.799276,43.463455,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cantina Mexicana</name><description><![CDATA[Mexican · Liérganes<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/eBsS5mP6189k5MNTA">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cantina-mexicana">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.7422698,43.345343,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa Ajero</name><description><![CDATA[Tapas &amp; pintxos · Santander · 942 218 386<br>Tapas and pintxos bar near Plaza del Cañadío with a lively tapeo atmosphere and a summer terrace with high tables.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.463079,-3.801235">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-ajero">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.801235,43.463079,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa Lita</name><description><![CDATA[Tapas &amp; pintxos · Santander · +34 942 36 48 30<br>Pintxo bar known as 'La Cocina del Pincho' on Paseo de Pereda, with a menu of around 300 different pinchos; queues at peak hours.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.462609,-3.797333">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-lita">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.797333,43.462609,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa Luisa</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Liérganes<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/hDb6jnv9HpLVby7NA">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-luisa">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.7448486,43.3434696,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa Poli</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Vidiago, Llanes (Asturias) · 985 41 12 17<br>Traditional Asturian cooking in an 1833 manor house around a central courtyard, open since 1996. Menu: chorizo in cider, Llanes anchovies, octopus, fabada, cachopo, T-bone, entrecote, lamb chops, cheeses and homemade desserts. Ample parking.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.398567,-4.686083">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-poli">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.686083,43.398567,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>El Bulín de la Tasca</name><description><![CDATA[Pizza (Argentine-style) · Santander<br>Argentine-style pizza place with vegan options (including vegan cheese and customisable toppings) and outdoor seating. Rated 4.4 on one guide (about 930 reviews); reviewers praise the friendly service and generous portions.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/8gvPB8tjPbpNrybf8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#el-bulin-de-la-tasca">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.7984261,43.4628827,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>El Carmelo</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Santander<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/1Qsysu6fS5n9FAEN6">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#el-carmelo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.7994963,43.4661759,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>El Cazurro</name><description><![CDATA[Bar / restaurant · €€ · 942 57 85 24<br>Coastal bar-restaurant with sea views from the dining room and terrace; short menu with a blackboard of daily fish and off-menu dishes. Known for rice dishes (incl. black rice), mejillones en salsa, guiso marinero, sea bass, octopus, croquetas and rabas. Repsol Solete; recommended by Jesus Sanchez (Cenador de Amos).<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.47273,-3.917251">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#el-cazurro">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.917251,43.47273,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>El Perdón</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Santillana del Mar<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/C4kZGALTDR6SGhUu8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#el-perdon">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1081178,43.389776,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Heladería Crepería Santillán</name><description><![CDATA[Ice cream / crêperie · Santillana del Mar<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/6sV5KuY5xuJhVcmq8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#heladeria-creperia-santillan">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1079071,43.3900822,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kandela</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Santander · €€€ · 942 52 65 83<br>Product-driven restaurant with a charcoal-grill focus, meat and fish as protagonists. Guests mention chuletón (especially ox), steak tartare, sweetbreads, ensaladilla rusa, chorizo brioche, flan and cheesecake. Upmarket, modern and stylish; good for dinner.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.464025,-3.797828">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#kandela">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.797828,43.464025,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Alpaquita</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Santander<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/zWJhdQ8qmRcQ568h9">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-alpaquita">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.8217109,43.4542155,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Bombi</name><description><![CDATA[Seafood · Santander · €€€–€€€€ · 942 213 028<br>Puertochico restaurant with about 90 years of history (formerly the sailors' tavern La Bombilla), specialising in fish and seafood. Classics: anchovies, marinated sea bass, bonito with tomato, fresh squid rabas, scorpionfish pudding. Upmarket Santander classic for fish and seafood; for a special occasion.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.464369,-3.796926">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-bombi">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.796926,43.464369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Casuca del Gorbea</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Miravalles, Torrelavega<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/GhyBU8j8mcpWJstc6">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-casuca-del-gorbea">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.0471576,43.3470764,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Gruta de José</name><description><![CDATA[Seafood · €€€ · 942 13 47 18<br>Seafood restaurant set in a sea-cave style interior in Santander's Barrio Pesquero; the star is Cantabrian centollo (spider crab), plus lobster, cigalas, percebes, daily fish and classics like rabas, croquetas and Santoña anchovies.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.450943,-3.819992">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-gruta-de-jose">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.819992,43.450943,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Herradura Food&amp;Drink</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Espinilla, Campoo de Suso<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/y3PDmWpmGWKD6rHQA">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-herradura-food-drink">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.224242,43.0214134,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Mano de Fátima</name><description><![CDATA[Spanish-Moroccan · Santander · +34 685 06 35 96<br>Small, lively Moroccan and Middle Eastern restaurant in Santander with many vegan options; chef Nabil Bour-qaiba. Reviewers praise the homemade food, generous portions and couscous (beef or chicken); muhammara with Arabic bread is a vegetarian-guide pick.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/FPosCmvkCN8137mu9">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-mano-de-fatima">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.7998651,43.4641283,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Parrilla de Prellezo</name><description><![CDATA[Asador (grill) · Prellezo, Val de San Vicente · 942 71 08 41<br>Grill restaurant specialising in grilled meats, good wine and homemade desserts; reviewers praise the aged chuleton (30-day), parrillada, cachopo, Prellezo tomatoes, ham-and-cecina croquetas and cheesecake. Terrace; dogs admitted.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.380303,-4.439802">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-parrilla-de-prellezo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.439802,43.380303,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Vinoteca</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Santander · €€€ · 942 07 57 41<br>Wine-focused restaurant in Puertochico, Santander, praised for staff, food and wine selection; Spanish/Mediterranean/fusion cooking. Rated 4.6 on Tripaligner (1,626 reviews).<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/kvhEYbM37gcsAqce8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#la-vinoteca">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.7977731,43.4631328,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Los Blasones</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Santillana del Mar<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/gSYVPL5TEqvP5ig88">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#los-blasones">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1078363,43.3893177,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mercado de la Esperanza</name><description><![CDATA[Market · Santander · 942 203 087<br>Historic Santander market opened in 1904 (architects Eduardo Reynals and Juan Moya), declared historic-artistic monument in 1977 and renovated in 2010, with about 80 stalls of meat, fish, seafood, produce, cheese, bread and coffee. A must for local produce, seafood and a proper Santander market experience.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.462788,-3.809979">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#mercado-de-la-esperanza">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.809979,43.462788,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mesón de Borleña</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Borleña, Cantabria<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/5icKZb2Uor7iCoaD8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#meson-de-borlena">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.9482536,43.2355973,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Montaña de Oro Sarón</name><description><![CDATA[Restaurant · Sarón, Santa María de Cayón<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/PeWGE33PaNgLuFAA8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#montana-de-oro-saron">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.853821,43.3249189,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mr. Wang</name><description><![CDATA[Chinese · Santander · €<br>Simple, casual Chinese restaurant with homemade cooking and an open kitchen. Reviewers recommend the arroz Mr. Wang, mapo tofu and dumplings; about €15 per person per one guide. Rated 8.2 on Gastroranking (about 340 opinions).<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/UD6w38Mi9gbYh5zQ7">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#mr-wang">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.8042647,43.4630508,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pausau</name><description><![CDATA[Seafood · Liencres, Piélagos · +34 942 13 10 51<br>Seafood-focused restaurant in Liencres with a panoramic terrace by the cliffs; Cantabrian sea produce, turbot, caldeirada, homemade croquettes and house desserts. Reviewers praise the views; some note it gets crowded and noisy.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/v26zf3JeghxfmhnV8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#pausau">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.9166883,43.4724925,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Peter &amp; Pan</name><description><![CDATA[Café / breakfast · Santander · 942 53 62 18<br>Bakery-cafe with a wide menu and attractive decor, popular with families; reviewers single out the coffee and the chocolate cookie.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.447412,-3.865888">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#peter-pan">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.865888,43.447412,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pollos a la Brasa Sabor Peruano</name><description><![CDATA[Peruvian rotisserie chicken · Santander<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/25R7B3sYXuboPta87">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#pollos-a-la-brasa-sabor-peruano">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.8163396,43.4554637,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sakura Santander</name><description><![CDATA[Japanese · Santander<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/xdFZMm5S8c1ePRdCA">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#sakura-santander">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.8415001,43.4385109,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Santa &amp; Co</name><description><![CDATA[Café / breakfast · Santander (centre) · +34 613 25 08 78<br>Relaxed, unpretentious cafe in central Santander for breakfast, brunch or an afternoon snack; founded by an architect and an economist. Reviewers single out tomato-and-avocado toast and coffee.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/rmVmhKhYok8scGzw6?g_st=ic">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#santa-co">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.803841,43.463575,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Santagloria Coffee &amp; Bakery</name><description><![CDATA[Café / breakfast · 942 369 430<br>Cafe and bakery near the Town Hall Square and Cathedral with a bright indoor cafe and a large quiet terrace; wide range of sweet and savoury pastries.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.462092,-3.81359">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#santagloria-coffee-bakery">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.81359,43.462092,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tierra Astur Águila (Colloto)</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Colloto, Siero · 985 791 228<br>Branch of the Tierra Astur cider-house group: Asturian cider house with traditional food.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.379878,-5.7904783">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#tierra-astur-aguila-colloto">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.7904783,43.379878,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tierra Astur Avilés</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Avilés · 984 833 038<br>Branch of the Tierra Astur cider-house group: Asturian cider house with traditional food.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.5552741,-5.9226823">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#tierra-astur-aviles">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.9226823,43.5552741,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tierra Astur El Vasco (Oviedo)</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Oviedo, Gran Bulevar El Vasco · 985 205 252<br>Branch of the Tierra Astur cider-house group: Asturian cider house with traditional food.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3655828,-5.842606">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#tierra-astur-el-vasco-oviedo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.842606,43.3655828,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tierra Astur Gascona (Oviedo)</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Oviedo, Calle Gascona<br>Branch of the Tierra Astur cider-house group: Asturian cider house with traditional food.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3643827,-5.8444892">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#tierra-astur-gascona-oviedo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.8444892,43.3643827,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tierra Astur Gascona Parrilla (Oviedo)</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Oviedo, Calle Gascona · 984 846 624<br>Branch of the Tierra Astur cider-house group: Asturian cider house with traditional food.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3642234,-5.8446305">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#tierra-astur-gascona-parrilla-oviedo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.8446305,43.3642234,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tierra Astur Poniente (Gijón)</name><description><![CDATA[Sidrería · Gijón, Playa de Poniente · 985 327 448<br>Branch of the Tierra Astur cider-house group: Asturian cider house with traditional food.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.5414993,-5.6749788">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#tierra-astur-poniente-gijon">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-5.6749788,43.5414993,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ylis</name><description><![CDATA[Asian (Thai / Chinese / Japanese) · Santander · 942 69 08 38<br>Asian restaurant in central Santander serving Thai, Chinese and Japanese dishes, with sushi fusion. Rated 8.1 on Gastroranking (about 250 opinions); reviewers praise the fresh food and varied menu.<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/C9XdsGfvi55SbrEu8">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#ylis">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.8035702,43.4640768,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Cultural Pass</name>
<Placemark><name>Antiguo Seminario Mayor de Comillas</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural site · Comillas<br>A vast Neo-Gothic former seminary overlooking Comillas, designed by Joan Martorell and later home to a pontifical university. Guided visits explore its church, halls and grounds.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38647,-4.29887">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#antiguo-seminario-mayor-de-comillas">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.29887,43.38647,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Arqueositio Cántabro-Romano de Camesa-Rebolledo</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural site · Camesa-Rebolledo<br>Two archaeological sites near Mataporquera linked to a Roman settlement founded after the Cantabrian Wars, close to a Roman road. A quiet stop that shows how Rome settled inland Cantabria.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=42.88735,-4.1584">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#arqueositio-cantabro-romano-de-camesa-rebolledo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1584,42.88735,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casas del Águila y la Parra</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural site · Santillana del Mar<br>Two neighbouring historic stone mansions on the main square of Santillana del Mar, open to visitors and free to enter. Easy to combine with a wander around the medieval town.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.39035,-4.10864">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casas-del-aguila-y-la-parra">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.10864,43.39035,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casona de Tudanca</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Tudanca<br>The family home of the writer and scholar José María de Cossío (until 1977), now a house-museum and library in the mountain village of Tudanca, famous for its cattle breed.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.15293,-4.37285">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casona-de-tudanca">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.37285,43.15293,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Centro de Arte Rupestre de Cantabria</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Puente Viesgo<br>An exhibition centre at the foot of Monte Castillo explaining Cantabria's cave art, through displays and guided visits. Free on the same day as a ticket for El Castillo or Las Monedas.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.29577,-3.96963">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#centro-de-arte-rupestre-de-cantabria">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.96963,43.29577,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Centro de Interpretación del Románico</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural site · Villacantid<br>A small interpretation centre in Villacantid, near Reinosa, explaining the Romanesque churches of southern Cantabria.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.00362,-4.20731">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#centro-de-interpretacion-del-romanico">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.20731,43.00362,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ciudad romana y Domus de Julióbriga</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural site · Retortillo<br>The most important Roman city in Cantabria, founded in 26 BC after the Cantabrian Wars on a hilltop near Retortillo. You can walk the streets and see the excavated Roman house, the Domus.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=42.98583,-4.11546">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#ciudad-romana-y-domus-de-juliobriga">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.11546,42.98583,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cueva de Chufín</name><description><![CDATA[Cave · Riclones<br>A cave above the meeting of the Lamasón and Nansa rivers with Palaeolithic paintings, listed by UNESCO. Open only seasonally, with very small groups and a short approach on foot.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.28322,-4.45828">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cueva-de-chufin">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.45828,43.28322,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cueva de Covalanas</name><description><![CDATA[Cave · Ramales de la Victoria<br>A Palaeolithic cave known for its red paintings of hinds (female deer), outlined in dots. It is part of the UNESCO World Heritage listing for the cave art of northern Spain, and only tiny groups are admitted.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.2456,-3.45207">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cueva-de-covalanas">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.45207,43.2456,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cueva de Cullalvera</name><description><![CDATA[Cave · Ramales de la Victoria<br>One of Cantabria's largest cave systems, with a walkway into the cave and Palaeolithic drawings on the walls. It is also the ticket office for nearby Covalanas.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.2557,-3.45814">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cueva-de-cullalvera">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.45814,43.2557,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cueva de El Castillo</name><description><![CDATA[Cave · Puente Viesgo<br>One of the oldest known cave-art sites in Europe, including a red disc dated to over 40,000 years ago. Guided visits of about an hour, and the ticket includes the Rock Art Centre.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.29222,-3.96549">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cueva-de-el-castillo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.96549,43.29222,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cueva de El Pendo</name><description><![CDATA[Cave · Escobedo de Camargo<br>A large prehistoric cave near Santander with a rich excavated record and Palaeolithic art, listed by UNESCO. Visited on a 45-minute guided tour.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38839,-3.91227">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cueva-de-el-pendo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.91227,43.38839,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cueva de Hornos de la Peña</name><description><![CDATA[Cave · San Felices de Buelna<br>A cave lived in for more than 30,000 years, from the Middle Palaeolithic to the Neolithic, with rock art and a UNESCO listing. Only four visitors per session.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.26134,-4.03002">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cueva-de-hornos-de-la-pena">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.03002,43.26134,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cueva de Las Monedas</name><description><![CDATA[Cave · Puente Viesgo<br>A cave in the Monte Castillo group, named after coins found there, decorated with black drawings of animals. Timed guided visits of small groups; the ticket includes the Rock Art Centre.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.28892,-3.96769">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cueva-de-las-monedas">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.96769,43.28892,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo de la Naturaleza de Cantabria</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Carrejo<br>A natural-history museum in an 18th-century mansion in Carrejo, near Cabezón de la Sal, with exhibits on Cantabria's wildlife and landscapes. Free on Sundays.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.29383,-4.23798">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-de-la-naturaleza-de-cantabria">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.23798,43.29383,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo de Prehistoria y Arqueología de Cantabria (MUPAC)</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Santander<br>Cantabria's main archaeology museum in Santander, built around finds from the region's famous prehistoric caves, with further collections from the ancient and medieval worlds.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.46226,-3.804">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-de-prehistoria-y-arqueologia-de-cantabria-mupac">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.804,43.46226,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo Etnográfico de Cantabria</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Muriedas<br>A museum in Muriedas about traditional Cantabrian life and culture, with guided visits and family workshops.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.42138,-3.85408">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-etnografico-de-cantabria">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.85408,43.42138,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo Marítimo del Cantábrico</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Santander<br>A museum and aquarium on the edge of Santander bay, covering marine life and the people of the Cantabrian Sea. A good rainy-day option for children.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.46332,-3.78368">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-maritimo-del-cantabrico">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.78368,43.46332,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Palacio y Capilla-Panteón de Sobrellano</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural site · Comillas<br>A Neo-Gothic palace built in the 1880s for the Marquess of Comillas, designed by Joan Martorell. The neighbouring chapel-pantheon, the family mausoleum, is a showpiece of Catalan Modernisme.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38353,-4.29438">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#palacio-y-capilla-panteon-de-sobrellano">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.29438,43.38353,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Torre de Pero Niño</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural site · San Felices de Buelna<br>A medieval tower (the Torre de la Aguilera) in San Felices de Buelna, now a museum about the life and times of the knight and naval commander Pero Niño.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.27811,-4.05237">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#torre-de-pero-nino">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.05237,43.27811,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Torre del Infantado</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Potes<br>A medieval fortified tower in the centre of Potes, at the foot of the Picos de Europa. A short visit that fits well with a walk around the town.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.15414,-4.62359">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#torre-del-infantado">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-cultura</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.62359,43.15414,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Family</name>
<Placemark><name>Laberinto de Tilde</name><description><![CDATA[Entrambasaguas, Campoo de Suso<br>An outdoor hedge maze in Campoo, best combined with another outing in the area rather than a dedicated drive.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.00972,-4.2816">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#laberinto-de-tilde">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-family</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.2816,43.00972,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Laberinto de Villapresente</name><description><![CDATA[Villapresente, Reocín<br>A seasonal outdoor hedge maze near Santillana del Mar, easy to combine with a visit to the town.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.36529,-4.11748">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#laberinto-de-villapresente">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-family</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.11748,43.36529,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Parque de la Naturaleza de Cabárceno</name><description><![CDATA[Obregón / Cabárceno<br>A large wildlife park in a former open-cast mine landscape near Santander. A full-day outing, with an annual pass worth considering.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.35552,-3.84135">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#parque-de-la-naturaleza-de-cabarceno">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-family</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.84135,43.35552,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Zoo de Santillana</name><description><![CDATA[Santillana del Mar<br>A zoo just outside Santillana del Mar; a half-day outing that pairs with the town and its museums.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38066,-4.10316">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#zoo-de-santillana">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-family</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.10316,43.38066,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Sights</name>
<Placemark><name>Camaleño</name><description><![CDATA[Day trip · Camaleño, Liébana<br>The Liébana municipality at the foot of the Picos de Europa; it includes Fuente Dé. A day-trip idea in your Notion.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.15084,-4.69388">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#camaleno">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.69388,43.15084,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa de Leonor de la Vega</name><description><![CDATA[Historic house · Santillana del Mar<br>Built at the end of the 15th century and substantially remodelled in the 16th, this house is attributed to Leonor de la Vega, mother of the Marquis of Santillana, Íñigo López de Mendoza.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.39067449631138,-4.107067358895488">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-de-leonor-de-la-vega">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.107067358895488,43.39067449631138,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa de los Abades</name><description><![CDATA[Historic house · Santillana del Mar · 942 81 88 98<br>Probably built at the end of the 17th century, this house originally belonged to the abbots of the Colegiata. Today it is known as the Casa de la Archiduquesa, having been the residence of Archduchess Margarita of Austria-Bourbon.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.39187453300494,-4.106194428207015">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-de-los-abades">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.106194428207015,43.39187453300494,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa de los Villa</name><description><![CDATA[Historic house · Santillana del Mar<br>A typical example of 18th-century town architecture, with pulpit-style balconies. In the mid-18th century it belonged to Francisco Antonio Pantaleón de Villa.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.389417612637835,-4.1087292042991574">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-de-los-villa">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1087292042991574,43.389417612637835,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Casa del Duque de Almodóvar del Río</name><description><![CDATA[Mansion · Comillas · 609 131 298<br>A magnificent 19th-century mansion, unique in Comillas because it is one of the few still owned by the original family, and it is still lived in: the owners spend their summer holidays there.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38775648475814,-4.291534423828125">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#casa-del-duque-de-almodovar-del-rio">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.291534423828125,43.38775648475814,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cementerio modernista de Comillas</name><description><![CDATA[Heritage · Comillas<br>Modernist cemetery on a hill facing the sea, set among the ruins of a former Gothic church and with an angel sculpture by Josep Llimona. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.390122,-4.293863">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#cementerio-modernista-de-comillas">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.293863,43.390122,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Centro Cultural El Espolón</name><description><![CDATA[Cultural centre · Comillas · 942 720 276<br>Built in the late 18th century for Juan Domingo González de la Reguera, Archbishop of Lima and a native of Comillas, to house a Chair of Latin Grammar; the Real Seminario Cántabro was founded here in 1802.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.386762374967695,-4.289442300796509">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#centro-cultural-el-espolon">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.289442300796509,43.386762374967695,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Colegiata de Santa Juliana</name><description><![CDATA[Heritage / church · Santillana del Mar<br>Romanesque collegiate church from the 12th century, the heart of Santillana del Mar. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.392289,-4.106163">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#colegiata-de-santa-juliana">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.106163,43.392289,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Convento de San Ildefonso</name><description><![CDATA[Convent · Santillana del Mar · 942 81 80 36<br>Built in 1667 in Baroque style, this convent was richer in income and property than Regina Coeli, and its community often took in young women from the region's leading families and great lineages.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38825921738098,-4.107906981575771">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#convento-de-san-ildefonso">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.107906981575771,43.38825921738098,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>El Capricho de Gaudí</name><description><![CDATA[Heritage / museum · Comillas · 942 72 03 65<br>Small modernist villa by Antoni Gaudí from his first period (1883–85), with rounded forms, a tall tower and sunflower tile decoration. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.383683,-4.292697">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#el-capricho-de-gaudi">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.292697,43.383683,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>El Hombre de los Vientos</name><description><![CDATA[Monument · Suances<br>Also called "Alma de Costa", this bronze by sculptor Jesús González de la Vega was unveiled in October 2010. Standing on a stone pedestal, the three-metre statue shows a man meeting the sea wind with open arms.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.43941,-4.0453449">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#el-hombre-de-los-vientos">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.0453449,43.43941,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ermita de San Esteban (Monte Corona)</name><description><![CDATA[Viewpoint · Monte Corona, Oyambre Natural Park (Comillas)<br>A small hermitage on a high point of Monte Corona (about 250 m) inside the Oyambre Natural Park. Next to it are a picnic area with tables and barbecues and a small viewpoint over the forest and the western Cantabrian coast; on clear days you can see San Vicente de la Barquera and the Picos de Europa. Reached by a paved forest road from La Hayuela. A pilgrimage (romeria) is held here around 3 August.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.34665,-4.29459">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#ermita-de-san-esteban-monte-corona">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.29459,43.34665,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ermita de Santa Justa</name><description><![CDATA[Heritage / coast · Ubiarco, Santillana del Mar<br>Small cove with the hermitage of Santa Justa built into the rock; the start of the coastal route to Puerto Calderón. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.425948,-4.097628">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#ermita-de-santa-justa">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.097628,43.425948,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jardín Histórico de Puente San Miguel</name><description><![CDATA[Garden · Puente San Miguel · 942 820 115<br>Owned by the Botín family, this estate was declared a Site of Cultural Interest in the Historic Garden category in 1986.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3635911,-4.0834218">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#jardin-historico-de-puente-san-miguel">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.0834218,43.3635911,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mirador de Covalruyo</name><description><![CDATA[Viewpoint · Soba<br>A viewpoint above the Asón valley in Soba, saved in Notion as a hiking/family idea.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.17896,-3.67692">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#mirador-de-covalruyo">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.67692,43.17896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mirador Playa de la Tablía</name><description><![CDATA[Viewpoint · Suances<br>This viewpoint stands above the beach of the same name, one of the wildest in Suances. It lies midway between Punta del Dichoso and Punta Ballota, with lovely views of the horizon and the cliffs.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.4348362,-4.0497917">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#mirador-playa-de-la-tablia">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.0497917,43.4348362,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Monumento al Marqués de Comillas</name><description><![CDATA[Monument · Comillas<br>Raised by the town of Comillas in memory of Antonio López y López, who returned from Cuba, set up his businesses in Barcelona and was made Marquis of his native Comillas by Alfonso XII in 1878.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3890641,-4.2912028">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#monumento-al-marques-de-comillas">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.2912028,43.3890641,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo de Altamira</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Santillana del Mar · 942 81 80 05<br>Museum and research centre for the Altamira cave art, with a permanent exhibition and activities for children and young people about how our ancestors lived. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.377406,-4.122397">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-de-altamira">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.122397,43.377406,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo de la Tortura</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Santillana del Mar · 942 840 273<br>A museum displaying more than 70 European instruments of torture and capital punishment, from the Middle Ages to the industrial era. Dogs are allowed.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.39049722029532,-4.107243476721192">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-de-la-tortura">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.107243476721192,43.39049722029532,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo Diocesano Regina Coeli</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Santillana del Mar · 942 840 317<br>Housed in the former Dominican friary of Regina Coeli ("Queen of Heaven"), the museum holds over 800 works from parishes across the region, notable for their popular character and dominated by sculpture, which with stonemasonry was the region's traditional craft.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38877007011115,-4.109069108963013">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-diocesano-regina-coeli">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.109069108963013,43.38877007011115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museo Jesús Otero</name><description><![CDATA[Museum · Santillana del Mar · 942 840 198<br>Sculptor Jesús Otero Oreña left his legacy to his home town in this museum and foundation beside the Colegiata de Santa Juliana.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.39183411353178,-4.1056787967681885">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#museo-jesus-otero">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1056787967681885,43.39183411353178,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Palacio de la familia Corro</name><description><![CDATA[Palace · San Vicente de la Barquera<br>This Renaissance palace, now the town hall of San Vicente de la Barquera, was commissioned in the 16th century by the inquisitor Antonio del Corro to shelter the town's sick poor.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3845,-4.4017">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#palacio-de-la-familia-corro">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.4017,43.3845,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Palacio de Peredo-Barreda</name><description><![CDATA[Palace · Santillana del Mar · 942 818 171<br>One of the town's most elegant and singular buildings, the ensemble comprises the palace, its annexed houses and their splendid garden.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3897435,-4.1085503">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#palacio-de-peredo-barreda">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1085503,43.3897435,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Palacio de Velarde</name><description><![CDATA[Palace · Santillana del Mar · 942 140 524 / 653618069<br>The finest example of Renaissance architecture in the town, built in the mid-16th century for Alonso de Velarde and also known as the Palacio de las Arenas. Its most important restoration was carried out in 1934.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.392298979896125,-4.105314613491813">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#palacio-de-velarde">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.105314613491813,43.392298979896125,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Parque de la Ribera</name><description><![CDATA[Park · Suances<br>A pretty park with impressive views over the Playa de la Ribera and the ría de San Martín.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.42888315122248,-4.034713495518549">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#parque-de-la-ribera">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.034713495518549,43.42888315122248,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Paseo por Novales y degustación de limonada</name><description><![CDATA[Walk · Novales<br>A stroll through this charming village, full of little channels. The walk is not complete without the obligatory lemonade or gin and tonic made with the area's prized lemons.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.37821043362102,-4.172613244244585">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#paseo-por-novales-y-degustacion-de-limonada">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.172613244244585,43.37821043362102,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Playa de Comillas</name><description><![CDATA[Beach · Comillas<br>Beach on the central coast. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.38921,-4.285652">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#playa-de-comillas">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.285652,43.38921,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Playa de Covachos</name><description><![CDATA[Beach · Santa Cruz de Bezana<br>A beach on the coast near Santander, about 3 km from Soto de la Marina, with a final stretch reached on foot.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.47267722284485,-3.9115123487699464">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#playa-de-covachos">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.9115123487699464,43.47267722284485,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Playa de la Concha</name><description><![CDATA[Beach · Suances<br>Beach on the central coast. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.435706,-4.043491">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#playa-de-la-concha">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.043491,43.435706,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Playa de los Locos</name><description><![CDATA[Beach · Suances<br>Beach on the central coast. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.438687,-4.046788">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#playa-de-los-locos">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.046788,43.438687,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Playa de Luaña</name><description><![CDATA[Beach · Cóbreces<br>Beach on the central coast. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.394027,-4.221225">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#playa-de-luana">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.221225,43.394027,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Playa de San Juan de la Canal</name><description><![CDATA[Beach · Santa Cruz de Bezana<br>A beach on the coast near Santander, 1 km from Soto de la Marina. It is well known for the busy party held nearby on the night of San Juan.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.47530886870769,-3.894356586610338">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#playa-de-san-juan-de-la-canal">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-3.894356586610338,43.47530886870769,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Playa de Tagle (El Sable)</name><description><![CDATA[Beach · Suances<br>Beach on the central coast. Listed in the Cantabria Costa Central visitor leaflet.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.427843,-4.093985">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#playa-de-tagle-el-sable">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.093985,43.427843,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Puerto de Comillas (El Muelle)</name><description><![CDATA[Harbour · Comillas<br>Comillas men seem to have taken up fishing on a significant scale only in the 16th century, because San Vicente de la Barquera held the exclusive right to fish the coast for two leagues east and west of its harbour.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.3908026,-4.290728">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#puerto-de-comillas-el-muelle">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.290728,43.3908026,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ría de San Martín de la Arena</name><description><![CDATA[Estuary · Suances<br>An estuary on Cantabria's central coast, between the municipalities of Suances, Polanco and Miengo, where the river Saja reaches the sea.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.4307094,-4.0361388">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#ria-de-san-martin-de-la-arena">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.0361388,43.4307094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ruta Cascadas de Toñanes</name><description><![CDATA[Walk · Toñanes<br>An easy walk that starts by the village of Toñanes, with just one tricky part: the final descent to the waterfall, which can be a little slippery for small children.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.40046127606476,-4.1986959939235025">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#ruta-cascadas-de-tonanes">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.1986959939235025,43.40046127606476,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Torre de los Velarde</name><description><![CDATA[Tower · Santillana del Mar<br>A Gothic tower built in the mid-15th century by García de Velarde, head of one of the town's great lineages. It was substantially remodelled in the early 17th century.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.39030370479751,-4.10751376808814">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#torre-de-los-velarde">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.10751376808814,43.39030370479751,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Torre del Merino</name><description><![CDATA[Tower · Santillana del Mar<br>A medieval Gothic tower of military character, built in the 14th century. It was the residence of the merino, the king's representative, after Santillana was made capital of the Asturias de Santillana in 1209, the largest jurisdiction in medieval Cantabria.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=43.39057283562903,-4.107915190178308">Open in Google Maps</a> · <a href="https://explorecantabria.fyi/#torre-del-merino">Open in the map app</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#s-attraction</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-4.107915190178308,43.39057283562903,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
